\pard\keepn \b\fs36\cf1 \{bmc bm0.bmp\}  Adjustable Height Measurement
\par \pard \plain\fs24 
\par This measurement facility comprises a related pair of \b horizontal lines\plain\fs24 . Each line may be adjusted in position and length.
\par \uldb \b Precision Adjustment\plain\b\fs24 {\v Precision_Adjustment}\plain\fs24  is available
\par \b    \plain\fs24 
\par \trowd\trgaph105\trleft-116 \cellx8495\cellx8995\cellx12055\pard\intbl\li355\fi-355\tx355 \b \{bmc bm1.bmp\}\tab \plain\ul\fs24 Click\plain\fs24 {\v CLICK@Sem.HLP} on the \b Adjustable Height Measurement Icon \plain\fs24 to switch the function on.
\par\intbl 
\par\intbl \b \{bmc bm1.bmp\}\plain\fs24 \tab Point to the \b Zone\plain\fs24  for which you want to place the Adjustable Height Measurement and click.
\par\intbl 
\par\intbl \b \{bmc bm1.bmp\}\plain\fs24 \tab Click on the \b rectangle\plain\fs24 , pick the \ul handle\plain\fs24 {\v Handles@Sem.HLP} and \ul drag\plain\fs24 {\v DRAG@Sem.HLP} it to size.
\par\intbl 
\par\intbl \b \{bmc bm1.bmp\}\plain\fs24 \tab Click on the \b upper line\plain\fs24 , pick the handle and place it.
\par\intbl 
\par\intbl \b \{bmc bm1.bmp\}\plain\fs24 \tab Click on the \b lower line\plain\fs24 , pick the handle and place it.
\par\intbl 
\par\intbl \b \{bmc bm1.bmp\}\plain\fs24 \tab Double clicking on one of the markers calls the \uldb \b Results Panel\plain\b\fs24 {\v Results_Panel_Parameters}\plain\fs24  which annotates the Adjustable Cursor Height.
\par\intbl 
\par\intbl \b \{bmc bm1.bmp\}\plain\fs24 \tab The data from this objects \uldb results panel\plain\fs24 {\v Results_Panel_Parameters} can be copied to the clipboard for insertion into a speadsheet. This is achieved using the \uldb Annotation Copy\plain\fs24 {\v Anntotation_to_Clipboard} Popup Menu item.
\par\intbl \cell\pard \pard\intbl\li355\fi-355\tx355 \cell\pard \pard\intbl\li355\fi-355\tx355 
\par\intbl 
\par\intbl \{bmc bm2.bmp\}
\par\intbl \b \cell\intbl\row
\pard\tx355 \plain\fs24 \{bmc bm3.bmp\}\tab The dimensional measurement is derived from the zone magnification hence when multiple zones are present both lines are brought into the same zone.
\par 
\par \pard\li355\fi-355\tx355 \{bmc bm4.bmp\}\tab There are 10 instances available.
