{\up $}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up $} Annotation Warning}
{\up #}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up #} Annotation_Warning}
\pard \b\fs36\cf1 Annotation Warning
\par \plain\fs24 \{bmc bm3.bmp\}  \b WARNING CONCERNING ANNOTATION
\par 
\par \plain\fs24 If it is required to save an image into a TIFF file and later to load and print it to hardcopy then do not include the magnification value when saving to file.
\par If the annotation (e.g. data zone) is merged into the image and saved to a TIFF file then the magnification will be that with reference to the display device. If the file is subsequently reloaded and printed then the magnification \b VALUE\plain\fs24  will not be correct for this media.
\par \pard 
\par NOTE: The facility is provided to fix the output magnification to be \uldb \b referenced to a Polaroid 545\plain\b\fs24 {\v 32AVUYD@leoserv.hlp}\plain\fs24 
\par 
\par For unambiguous magnification use a \uldb Micron Marker\plain\fs24 {\v Micron_Marker}.
\par 
\par 
\par However, the file will contain the pixel sizes for each zone on the reloaded image so that the correct magnification can be re-established using \uldb Zone Magnification\plain\fs24 {\v Zone_Magnification}.
\par 
\par For measurement on imported TIFF files also observe \uldb \b Measurement Warning\plain\b\fs24 {\v Measurement_Warning}\plain\fs24 .
\par \page
{\up $}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up $} Anntotation to Clipboard}
{\up #}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up #} Anntotation_to_Clipboard}
{\up >}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up >} main}
\pard\keepn {\up K}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up K} Angular}
\b\fs36\cf1 Annotation to Clipboard
\par \pard \plain\fs24 
\par These functions perform Cut, Copy and Paste to/from the memory with selected annotation objects similar to Clipboard usage in Windows. 
\par 
\par Ensure first that all of the objects that are to be \b Cut\plain\fs24 , \b Copied\plain\fs24  or \b Pasted\plain\fs24  are \uldb selected\plain\fs24 {\v Object_Selection}. To bring up the Annotation menu, right click the mouse button \i outside\plain\fs24  any of the selected objects (as right clicking on any of the selected objects brings up the objects \uldb \b properties\plain\b\fs24 {\v Object_Properties}\plain\fs24  popup menu).
\par \pard 
\par \b\fs28 Cut:
\par \plain\fs24 Store the selected \uldb \b annotation objects\plain\b\fs24 {\v Object_Selection}\plain\fs24  in memory and remove them from the overlay plane.
\par 
\par \b\fs28 Copy:
\par \plain\fs24 Store the selected annotation objects in memory but leave them on the overlay plane too.
\par 
\par \pard\li225 \ul Note :\plain\fs24  When performing a \b Copy\plain\fs24  operation on any of the following \uldb measurement objects results panels\plain\fs24 {\v Results_Panel_Parameters}, the measurement data associated with them is copied to the clipboard in text format (Only the data appearing in the selected results panel will be copied. For the profile and histogram objects, ensure that the profile graphic or histogram graphic is selected before performing the copy function) :
\par 
\par \pard\li555\fi-355\tx555 1.\tab \uldb Point to Point\plain\fs24 {\v Point_to_Point} 
\par 2.\tab \uldb Stored Vector Profile\plain\fs24 {\v Stored_Vector_Profile} (Optional Profile Width, followed by profile image data values 0..255, one data value per pixel covered).
\par 3.\tab \uldb Stored Histogram\plain\fs24 {\v Stored_Data_Histogram} (A set of 256 values, each containing the pixel count for bin n where n = 0..255).
\par 4.\tab \uldb Angular\plain\fs24 {\v Angular_Measurement} 
\par 5.\tab \uldb Radial\plain\fs24 {\v Radial_Measurement}
\par 6.\tab \uldb Line Width\plain\fs24 {\v Line_Width}
\par 
\par \pard\li225\tx555 This special feature allows applications such as spreadsheets to graph/accumulate the data in their own special format, directly from the SEM User Interface. Note that all values are in standard engineering units (Amps, Metres, Volts, Degrees).
\par \pard\li225\tx555 
\par \pard\tx555 \b\fs28 Paste:
\par \pard\tx555 \plain\fs24 Copy the annotation objects which have been copied or pasted previously to the overlay plane.
\par \pard\tx555 
\par \pard\tx355 \{bmc bm3.bmp\}\tab The \uldb \b Data Zone\plain\b\fs24 {\v Data_Zone}\plain\fs24  is also cut if it was selected. You can regain the Data Zone by pasting it back.
\par \page
