\par \pard \plain\fs24 
\par \trowd\trgaph105\trleft-116 \cellx6795\cellx7295\cellx12055\pard\intbl The \uldb \b Annotation Settings popup menu\plain\b\fs24 {\v Annotation_Settings}\plain\fs24  allows quick and easy access to a number of control functions to edit and manipulate the annotation on the image.
\par\intbl \par\pard \pard\intbl\li355\fi-355\tx355 \b \{bmc bm1.bmp\}\plain\fs24 \tab Switch on the \uldb \b Annotation Toolbar\plain\b\fs24 {\v Calling_the_Annotation_Toolbar}\plain\fs24  
\par\intbl 
\par\intbl \b \{bmc bm1.bmp\}\tab \plain\fs24 \{bmc bm8.bmp\}  \ul Click\plain\fs24 {\v CLICK@Sem.HLP} in the \uldb \b Image Window\plain\b\fs24 {\v GIRNF0@Sem.HLP}\plain\fs24  with the right mouse button. The \uldb \b Annotation Settings Popup Menu\plain\b\fs24 {\v Annotation_Settings}\plain\fs24  opens. Choose the \b Annotation \{bmc bm1.bmp\}\plain\fs24  menu item.
\par\intbl 
\par\intbl \{bmc bm4.bmp\}\tab If Image Manager is not in \uldb \b Select Mode\plain\b\fs24 {\v Select_Mode}\plain\fs24 , then the right mouse button calls the \uldb \b Utility Popup Menu\plain\b\fs24 {\v Utility_Popup_Menu}\plain\fs24  instead, and the \b Annotation \{bmc bm1.bmp\}\plain\fs24  option is replaced by a \b Commands \{bmc bm1.bmp\}\plain\fs24  menu item.
\par\intbl \par\pard \pard\intbl\tx355 The user may define his own settings, store them on disk and load them back again via the \uldb \b Annotation Options...\plain\b\fs24 {\v The_Annotation_Options_Panel}\plain\fs24  Menu item.\par\pard \pard\intbl\tx355 \par\pard \pard\intbl\tx355 \uldb \b Detailed information\plain\b\fs24 {\v Changing_Annotation_Settings}\plain\fs24  is provided on each of the topics shown in the panel on the right. \par\pard \pard\intbl\tx355 \par\pard \pard\intbl\tx355 \{bmc bm10.bmp\}\tab Point to the topic of interest. When the cursor changes from \{bmc bm37.bmp\}to \{bmc bm38.bmp\}help is available. Click to present the additional information.
