\pard\keepn \b\fs36\cf1 Context Sensitive Popup Menu
\par \pard \plain\fs24 
\par Depending on the current \uldb \b Image Manager Operating Mode\plain\b\fs24 {\v Image_Manager_Operating_Mode}\plain\fs24 , (either \uldb \b Select Mode\plain\b\fs24 {\v Select_Mode}\plain\i\ul\fs24  \plain\fs24 or \uldb \b Mouse Control Mode\plain\b\fs24 {\v Mouse_Control_Mode}\plain\fs24 ) \ul clicking\plain\fs24 {\v CLICK@Sem.HLP} the right mouse button in the SEM \uldb \b Image Window\plain\b\fs24 {\v GIRNF0@Sem.HLP}\plain\fs24  will cause a Pop-up Menu to be displayed. 
\par 
\par The contents of this menu is determined by the above Image Manager operating mode, and whether or not the cursor is over an \uldb \b Image Manager Object\plain\b\fs24 {\v Image_Manager_Objects}\plain\fs24  (when the mouse cursor is over an object, it must usually first be selected). Each of the types of Pop-up Menu are discussed below:
\par \pard 
\par \{bmc bm8.bmp\} Right clicking on the Image in Image Manager \uldb \b Select Mode\plain\b\fs24 {\v Select_Mode} \plain\fs24 displays the \uldb \b Annotation Settings Popup Menu\plain\b\fs24 {\v Annotation_Settings}\plain\fs24 
\par 
\par \{bmc bm8.bmp\} Right clicking on the Image in \uldb \b Mouse Control Mode \plain\b\fs24 {\v Mouse_Control_Mode} \plain\fs24 displays the \uldb \b Utility Popup Menu\plain\b\fs24 {\v Utility_Popup_Menu}
\par \plain\fs24 
\par \{bmc bm8.bmp\} Right clicking on a \uldb \b Selected Image Manager Object\plain\b\fs24 {\v Objects_Properties_Menu}\plain\fs24 
\par \page
{\up $}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up $} Copy Selected Annotation}
{\up #}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up #} Copy_Selected_Annotation}
{\up >}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up >} main}
\pard\keepn \b\fs36\cf1 Copy Selected Annotation
\par \pard \plain\fs24 
\par Accessed via the \uldb \b Annotation Settings\plain\b\fs24 {\v Annotation_Settings} \plain\fs24 Popup Menu, this function copies \uldb \b selected objects\plain\b\fs24 {\v Object_Selection}\plain\fs24  into a temporary file ready for pasting back into the \uldb \b Image Window\plain\b\fs24 {\v GIRNF0@Sem.HLP}\plain\fs24  as new objects. 
\par 
\par The System Clipboard is \b not\plain\fs24  used for this operation
\par 
\par Use the \uldb \b Undo Function\plain\b\fs24 {\v Undo_Last_Edit_Delete}\plain\fs24  to restore any annotation objects affected by this function.
\par \page
{\up $}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up $} Creation of Objects}
{\up #}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up #} Creation_of_Objects}
{\up >}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up >} main}
\pard\keepn {\up K}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up K} Brush Settings}
\b\fs36\cf1 Creation of Objects
\par \pard \plain\fs24 
\par To create an object, bring up the \uldb \b Annotation Toolbar\plain\b\fs24 {\v Calling_the_Annotation_Toolbar}\plain\fs24  by 
\par 
\par \{bmc bm28.bmp\}  pressing \b <CTRL+A>\plain\fs24  or \{bmc bm10.bmp\} selecting \b Edit\plain\fs24  then \b Annotation\plain\fs24  from the \uldb \b Menu Bar\plain\b\fs24 {\v 8ZP0K4@Sem.HLP}\plain\fs24 . 
\par 
\par Most of the Image Manager Objects follow the same principle when creating them, so the example below shows how to create an Ellipse Annotation Object :
\par \trowd\trgaph105\trleft-116 \cellx8495\cellx12685\pard\intbl\li355\fi-355\tx355 \b \{bmc bm1.bmp\}\plain\fs24 \tab From the toolbar click the grey ellipse \{bmc bm18.bmp\}. Note that the button presses down and stays down.
\par\intbl 
\par\intbl \b \{bmc bm1.bmp\}\plain\fs24 \tab Move the mouse pointer to the part of the image where the top left of the object is to be placed.
\par\intbl 
\par\intbl \b \{bmc bm1.bmp\}\plain\fs24 \tab Press the left mouse button and hold it down.\cell\pard \pard\intbl\li355\fi-355\tx355 \pard\intbl \{bmc bm40.bmp\}\cell\intbl\row
\pard\li355\fi-355\tx355 \b \{bmc bm1.bmp\}\plain\fs24 \tab Now \ul drag\plain\fs24 {\v DRAG@Sem.HLP} the mouse left and down, Image Manager draws a 'ghost' object of the ellipse that follows or 'tracks' the mouse, the SEM UIF \uldb \b Status Bar\plain\b\fs24 {\v RDJHU5@Sem.HLP}\plain\fs24  will display object dimensions as the mouse is dragged.
\par 
\par \b \{bmc bm1.bmp\}\plain\fs24 \tab When the ellipse is at a reasonable size, let go of the left mouse button
\par 
\par \b \{bmc bm1.bmp\}\plain\fs24 \tab Image Manager creates the object in place of the 'ghost' object.
\par 
\par \{bmc bm4.bmp\} Note also that in \uldb \b Select Mode\plain\b\fs24 {\v Select_Mode}\plain\fs24 , the object is shown to be \i selected\plain\fs24  as it it highlighted by selection \ul handles\plain\fs24 {\v Handles@Sem.HLP}.
\par \pard\tx355 
\par \pard\li355\fi-355\tx355 \{bmc bm4.bmp\} \b Note\plain\i\fs24  : \plain\fs24 Most objects have a default size if the mouse is simply clicked once on the image to denote the top left corner of the object. If the object does not create however, the initial 'ghost' object  may need to be dragged to at least a certain size.
\par \page
