{\up $}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up $} Filename Format}
{\up #}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up #} Filename_Format}
\pard \b\fs36\cf1 Filename Format
\par \plain\fs24 The filename may be constructed in a number of ways as defined on the Export \uldb Settings\plain\fs24 {\v Export_Tiff_Settings} tab.
\par 
\par Select \b Photo No\plain\fs24 . This uses the Photo No. parameter as the filename. It is automatically incremented for every image export (File export, Print or HRRU Photograph)
\par 
\par Select\b  File No.\plain\fs24 . This uses the 7 digit File No. parameter which is incremented on each file export.
\par 
\par Select \b Max 8 Chars \plain\fs24 to restrict the filename size if the files are for use on systems running Windows 3.1
\par \pard Select \b Max 30 Chars\plain\fs24  if more descriptive filenames are required.
\par 
\par If \b Photo No\plain\fs24 .or \b File No\plain\fs24  are not used as filename the filename is constructed by appending a number of digits to the base \b filename\plain\fs24  on the \uldb Save\plain\fs24 {\v Export_TIFF_Save} tab.
\par 
\par Select the number of digits to be appended.
\par 
\par Select the initial value of the incrementing number in the \b Next\plain\fs24  box.
\par 
\par Note that the \b Photo No.\plain\fs24  and\b  File No.\plain\fs24  parameters may be displayed as annotation
\par \page
{\up $}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up $} Fixed Micron Bar}
{\up #}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up #} 13.IZL9}
{\up >}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up >} main}
\pard\keepn \b\fs36\cf1 \{bmc bm58.bmp\}  Fixed Micron Bar
\par \pard \plain\fs24 This comprises a horizontal bar which indicates the size of an object in the image. Above the bar is displayed it's length\b .
\par \plain\fs24 If the image is in a mode comprising multiple \uldb \b zones\plain\b\fs24 {\v Zone}\plain\fs24  then the micron marker displays the zone magnification of the zone identified by the pixel at the top left corner of the text. (i.e. the top left corner of the box displayed when moving the object).
\par \trowd\trgaph105\trleft-116 \cellx9635\cellx13535\pard\intbl\li355\fi-355\tx355 
\par\intbl \b \{bmc bm1.bmp\}\tab \plain\ul\fs24 Click\plain\fs24 {\v CLICK@Sem.HLP} on the \b Fixed Micron Marker Icon \plain\fs24 to switch the function on.
\par\intbl 
\par\intbl \b \{bmc bm1.bmp\}\plain\fs24 \tab Point to the \b Zone\plain\fs24  for which you want to show the Fixed Micron Marker and click.\par\pard \pard\intbl\tx355 The micron marker represents a fixed dimension, and may therefore extend off the screen if the magnification is too large or may shrink to a single pixel length if the magnification is too low. Editing the Micron marker permits the size to be changed.\par\pard \pard\intbl\tx355 \par\pard \pard\intbl\li355\fi-355\tx355 \b \{bmc bm1.bmp\}\plain\fs24 \tab Insert the value into the text field of the \b Annotation Micron Measurement\plain\fs24  panel.
\par\intbl 
\par\intbl \b \{bmc bm1.bmp\}\plain\fs24 \tab \b <OK>\plain\fs24  sets the value,\b  <Cancel>\plain\fs24  leaves the panel without change.
\par\intbl 
\par\intbl \b \{bmc bm1.bmp\}\plain\fs24 \tab The Fixed Micron Marker will be shown at the selected place of the Image Window \cell\pard \pard\intbl\li355\fi-355\tx355 \pard\intbl\tx355 \par\pard \pard\intbl\tx355 \{bmc bm59.bmp\}\par\pard \pard\intbl\tx355 \par\pard \pard\intbl\tx355 \{bmc bm60.bmp\}\par\pard \pard\intbl \cell\intbl\row
