\par \pard\tx355 \{bmc bm62.bmp\}
\par \pard\tx355 
\par \pard\tx355 The object can be deleted by selecting the object and pressing the \b <DELETE>\plain\fs24  key, or by choosing the \b Delete\plain\fs24  option from its \uldb \b Properties Popup Menu.\plain\b\fs24 {\v Objects_Properties_Menu}\plain\fs24 
\par \page
{\up $}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up $} HRRU Photo}
{\up #}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up #} HRRU_Photo}
\pard\keepn \b\fs36\cf1 HRRU Photo
\par \pard \plain\fs24 
\par \cf2 This panel allows the operator to select how a photo exposure will be performed.  It also shows the current status of the HRRU.\plain\fs24 
\par \trowd\trgaph105\trleft-116 \cellx6765\cellx13745\pard\intbl\li355\fi-355\tx355 \cf2 \{bmc bm1.bmp\}\tab Use\b  Photo\plain\fs24\cf2  to start the exposure.\par\pard \pard\intbl\tx355 The progress bar indicates how far an individual exposure has progressed.\par\pard \pard\intbl\tx355 \par\pard \pard\intbl\li355\fi-355\tx355 \{bmc bm1.bmp\}\tab \b Abort Photo\plain\fs24\cf2  can be used to terminate an exposure before it completes.
\par\intbl \par\pard \pard\intbl\tx355 Completion of the exposure is indicated by \b Camera Status = Idle.\par\pard \pard\intbl\tx355 \par\pard \pard\intbl \plain\fs24\cf2 Other information fields include:\cell\pard \pard\intbl \{bmc bm57.bmp\}\cell\intbl\row
\pard \b Photo Number\plain\fs24\cf2  which is incremented each time an image is exported. Double clicking in the field allows input of a number.
\par 
\par \b Photo Time\plain\fs24\cf2  as set in the \b Photo Settings Dialog\plain\fs24\cf2  panel.
\par 
\par If you use direct developing film the \uldb \b Photo Development Timer\plain\b\fs24\cf2 {\v Photo_Development_Timer}\plain\fs24\cf2 .helps for proper timing.
\par 
\par Also see\uldb  \b Photo Selection Dialog\plain\b\fs24\cf2 {\v Photo_Selection_Dialog} \plain\fs24\cf2 and observe \b Parameter Control Analogue \plain\fs24\cf2 for parameter input.
\par \page
