{\up #}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up #} FYFERF}
{\up >}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up >} main}
\pard\keepn \b\fs36\cf1 \{bmc bm63.bmp\}  Height Measurement
\par \pard \plain\fs24 
\par This measurement facility comprises a related pair of \b horizontal lines\plain\fs24 . Each line may be adjusted in position. \uldb \b Precision Adjustment\plain\b\fs24 {\v Precision_Adjustment}\plain\fs24  is available.
\par 
\par \trowd\trgaph105\trleft-116 \cellx9065\cellx13255\pard\intbl\li355\fi-355\tx355 \b \{bmc bm1.bmp\}\tab \plain\ul\fs24 Click\plain\fs24 {\v CLICK@Sem.HLP} on the \b Height Measurement Icon \plain\fs24 to switch the function on.
\par\intbl 
\par\intbl \b \{bmc bm1.bmp\}\plain\fs24 \tab Click on the \b left line\plain\fs24 , pick the \ul handle\plain\fs24 {\v Handles@Sem.HLP} and place it.
\par\intbl 
\par\intbl \b \{bmc bm1.bmp\}\plain\fs24 \tab Click on the \b right line\plain\fs24 , pick the handle and place it.
\par\intbl 
\par\intbl \b \{bmc bm1.bmp\}\plain\fs24 \tab Double clicking on one of the markers calls the \uldb \b Results Panel\plain\b\fs24 {\v Results_Panel_Parameters}\plain\fs24  which annotates the Cursor Width.
\par\intbl \cell\pard \pard\intbl\li355\fi-355\tx355 \pard\intbl \{bmc bm64.bmp\}\cell\intbl\row
\pard\tx355 \{bmc bm3.bmp\}\tab The dimensional measurement is derived from the zone magnification hence when multiple zones are present both lines are shortened into the same zone.
\par 
\par \pard\li355\fi-355\tx355 \{bmc bm4.bmp\}\tab There is one instance available.
\par \pard\tx355 
\par \pard\li355\fi-355\tx355 See also \uldb \b Retrospective Measurement\plain\b\fs24 {\v Retrospective_Measurement}\plain\fs24 . \tab \tab \uldb \b Properties of Height Measurement\plain\b\fs24 {\v Properties_of_Height_Measurement}\plain\fs24 
