\pard\keepn \b\fs36\cf1 Hidden Objects
\par \pard \plain\fs24 
\par When an object is hidden, it is as if the object were temporarily deleted. No \uldb \b selection\plain\b\fs24 {\v Object_Selection}\plain\fs24  can be made on these objects, and they cannot be deleted whilst hidden.
\par 
\par The SEM \uldb \b Menu Bar\plain\b\fs24 {\v 8ZP0K4@Sem.HLP}\plain\fs24  can be used to access the \uldb \b Hide Annotation\plain\b\fs24 {\v Hide_Annotation}\plain\fs24  objects or \uldb \b Unhide Annotation\plain\b\fs24 {\v Unhide_Annotation}\plain\fs24  objects functions.
\par \page
{\up $}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up $} Hide Annotation}
{\up #}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up #} Hide_Annotation}
{\up >}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up >} main}
\pard\keepn \b\fs36\cf1 Hide Annotation
\par \pard\tx355 \plain\fs24 
\par This function allows to hide annotation objects in a differentiated way:
\par 
\par \b\fs28 Hide Selected Objects:
\par \plain\fs24 All objects which are selected (\ul handles\plain\fs24 {\v Handles@Sem.HLP} are displayed) become invisible.
\par 
\par \{bmc bm28.bmp\}\tab The short cut from the keyboard is \b <CTRL + H>\plain\fs24 
\par 
\par \pard\tx355 \b\fs28 Hide Standard Annotation:
\par \pard\tx355 \plain\fs24 Standard annotation objects (text, parameter annotation, bitmap, line, rectangle, ellipse, sticky panel, TIFF data) become invisible.
\par \pard\tx355 
\par \pard\tx355 \b\fs28 Hide Measurement Annotation:
\par \pard\tx355 \plain\fs24 Measurement annotation objects (Micron Bars, Point to Point, Angular, Line Width, Circular, Horizontal, Vertical, Vector Profile) become invisible.
\par \pard\tx355 
\par \pard\tx355 \b\fs28 Hide Data Zone Annotation:
\par \pard\tx355 \plain\fs24 The Data Zone becomes invisible.
\par \pard\tx355 
\par \pard\tx355 \b\fs28 Hide Image Selection Area(s):
\par \pard\tx355 \plain\fs24 The selected areas are set invisible.
\par \pard\tx355 
\par \pard\tx355 \b\fs28 Hide Image Selection Handles:
\par \pard\tx355 \plain\fs24 Image Selection Handles are set invisible.
\par \pard\tx355 
\par \pard\tx355 \b\fs28 Hide Results Panels:
\par \pard\tx355 \plain\fs24 Measurement Objects Results Panels are set invisible.
\par \pard\tx355 
\par \pard\tx355 \b\fs28 Hide All:
\par \pard\tx355 \plain\fs24 Sets all of the above annotation objects invisible.
\par \page
