\pard\keepn \b\fs36\cf1 Image Manager Objects
\par \pard \plain\fs24 
\par A special graphical object that can be \uldb \b created\plain\b\fs24 {\v Creation_of_Objects}\plain\fs24  or \uldb \b selected\plain\b\fs24 {\v Object_Selection}\plain\fs24  in the \uldb \b Image Window\plain\b\fs24 {\v GIRNF0@Sem.HLP}\plain\fs24 . 
\par 
\par The \uldb \b Image Manager Toolbar\plain\b\fs24 {\v Calling_the_Annotation_Toolbar}\plain\fs24  is a good place to select object for creation, however, certain objects such as \uldb \b Text Annotation\plain\b\fs24 {\v Text_Annotation}\plain\fs24  or \uldb \b Point to Point Measurement\plain\b\fs24 {\v Point_to_Point}\plain\fs24  objects can be created from the SEM \uldb \b Menu Bar\plain\b\fs24 {\v 8ZP0K4@Sem.HLP}\plain\fs24 .
\par 
\par The objects may be used for measurement, SEM Parameter adjustment, or as simple annotation of a feature of interest on the Image.
\par \pard 
\par Most Image Manager objects have attributes or \uldb \b properties\plain\b\fs24 {\v Object_Properties}\plain\fs24  that can be changed by the user.
\par \page
{\up $}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up $} Image Manager Operating Mode}
