{\up >}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up >} main}
\pard\keepn \b\fs36\cf1 Image Manager Operating Mode
\par \pard \plain\fs24 
\par This mode determines the action taken by mouse clicks on the \uldb \b Image Window\plain\b\fs24 {\v GIRNF0@Sem.HLP}\plain\fs24  and is not related to the current SEM Operating Mode. There are two main modes of operation :
\par 
\par \{bmc bm7.bmp\}  \fs28 Select Mode
\par \fs24 
\par \pard\li355 When the Select Mode button is pressed on the \uldb \b Annotation Toolbar\plain\b\fs24 {\v Calling_the_Annotation_Toolbar}\plain\fs24 , Image Manager Object Selection can take place.\fs28 
\par \pard \fs24 
\par \{bmc bm65.bmp\}  \fs28 Mouse Control Mode
\par \fs24 
\par \pard\li355 When the Mouse Control Mode button is pressed on the Toolbar, Image Manager acts as if the toolbar has been switched off.\fs28 
\par \pard \fs24 
\par Both these modes affect the \uldb \b Context Sensitive Popup Menu\plain\b\fs24 {\v Context_Sensitive_Popup_Menu}\plain\fs24 .
\par \page
