{\up $}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up $} Line Width}
{\up #}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up #} 123AG2K}
{\up >}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up >} main}
\pard\keepn \b\fs36\cf1 \{bmc bm81.bmp\}  Line Width
\par \pard \plain\fs24 
\par The line width measurement object is a rectangle which may be adjusted in height, width and angle. \uldb \b Precision Adjustment\plain\b\fs24 {\v Precision_Adjustment}\plain\fs24  is available.
\par 
\par \trowd\trgaph105\trleft-116 \cellx9065\cellx13815\pard\intbl\li355\fi-355\tx355 \b \{bmc bm1.bmp\}\tab \plain\ul\fs24 Click\plain\fs24 {\v CLICK@Sem.HLP} on the \b Line Width Icon \plain\fs24 to switch the function on.
\par\intbl 
\par\intbl \b \{bmc bm1.bmp\}\plain\fs24 \tab Point to the \b Zone\plain\fs24  for which you want to place the Line Width Rectangle and click.
\par\intbl 
\par\intbl \b \{bmc bm1.bmp\}\plain\fs24 \tab Pick the \ul handles\plain\fs24 {\v Handles@Sem.HLP} of the \b first side La n\plain\fs24  and place them.
\par\intbl 
\par\intbl \b \{bmc bm1.bmp\}\plain\fs24 \tab Pick the handles of the \b second side Lb n\plain\fs24  and place them.
\par\intbl 
\par\intbl \b \{bmc bm1.bmp\}\plain\fs24 \tab Double clicking on one of the lines calls the \uldb \b Results Panel\plain\b\fs24 {\v Results_Panel_Parameters}\plain\fs24  containing the measurement parameters which are:
\par\intbl \b \tab La n \plain\fs24 dimension of the\b  first side\plain\fs24  of the rectangle, 
\par\intbl \tab \b Lb n \plain\fs24 dimension of the\b  second side\plain\fs24  of the rectangle and
\par\intbl \tab \b Lc n \plain\fs24 angle\b  \plain\fs24 of the first side to the scan direction
\par\intbl \tab \b Ld n\plain\fs24  The area of the rectangle
\par\intbl \tab where \b n\plain\fs24  is the instance identifier (i.e. 1 for first object created, 2 for second object)
\par\intbl 
\par\intbl \b \{bmc bm1.bmp\}\plain\fs24 \tab The data from this objects \uldb results panel\plain\fs24 {\v Results_Panel_Parameters} can be copied to the clipboard for insertion into a speadsheet. This is achieved using the \uldb Annotation Copy\plain\fs24 {\v Anntotation_to_Clipboard} Popup Menu item.\cell\pard \pard\intbl\li355\fi-355\tx355 \pard\intbl \{bmc bm82.bmp\}\cell\intbl\row
\pard\li355\fi-355\tx355 
\par \pard\tx355 \{bmc bm3.bmp\}\tab The dimensional measurement is derived from the zone magnification hence when multiple zones are present the rectangle must wholly lie within a zone. If the rectangle is moved so that it spans zones the dimensional values are set to zero and a \b ? \plain\fs24 is annotated.
\par 
\par \pard\li355\fi-355\tx355 See also \uldb \b Retrospective Measurement\plain\b\fs24 {\v Retrospective_Measurement}\plain\fs24 . \tab \tab \uldb \b Properties of Line Width Measurement\plain\b\fs24 {\v Properties_of_Line_Width_Measurement}\plain\fs24 
