{\up >}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up >} main}
\pard\keepn \b\fs36\cf1 \{bmc bm88.bmp\}  Micron Marker
\par \pard \plain\fs24 
\par This comprises a horizontal bar which indicates the size of an object in the image. Above the bar is displayed it's length\b .
\par \plain\fs24 The micon marker is self sizing in that the bar has minimum and maximum lengths. If the magnification is changed such that these limits would be exceeded the length represented by the bar is changed to a whole number which would permit the bar to lie within limits.
\par 
\par \trowd\trgaph105\trleft-116 \cellx9065\cellx11835\pard\intbl\li355\fi-355\tx355 \b \{bmc bm1.bmp\}\tab \plain\ul\fs24 Click\plain\fs24 {\v CLICK@Sem.HLP} on the \b Micron Marker Icon \plain\fs24 to switch the function on.
\par\intbl 
\par\intbl \b \{bmc bm1.bmp\}\plain\fs24 \tab Point to the \b Zone\plain\fs24  for which you want to show the Micron Marker and click.
\par\intbl 
\par\intbl \b \{bmc bm1.bmp\}\plain\fs24 \tab The Micron Marker will be shown at the selected place of the Image Window .
\par\intbl \b \{bmc bm1.bmp\}\plain\fs24 \tab Click on \b Annotation Mode Icon \{bmc bm7.bmp\} \plain\fs24 to leave the Micron Marker Mode.
\par\intbl \b 
\par\intbl \{bmc bm1.bmp\}\plain\fs24 \tab  The Micron Marker Annotation can be picked up \ul dragged\plain\fs24 {\v DRAG@Sem.HLP} into the required \b position\plain\fs24 . Make sure to place the annotation not over another zone.\cell\pard \pard\intbl\li355\fi-355\tx355 \pard\intbl\tx355 \par\pard \pard\intbl\tx355 \par\pard \pard\intbl \{bmc bm94.bmp\}\cell\intbl\row
\pard\li355\fi-355\tx355 
\par See also \uldb \b Retrospective Measurement\plain\b\fs24 {\v Retrospective_Measurement}\plain\fs24 . 
\par 
\par \{bmc bm28.bmp\}  The keyboard can be used to adjust the currently highlighted selection handle. This feature is especially useful for fine adjustments.
\par 
\par \{bmc bm4.bmp\}This object cannot extend beyond the image display area boundary. Where the marker straddles a \uldb zone\plain\fs24 {\v Zone} boundary, the zone used for the measurement is taken as the zone that the top left corner of the marker is in.
\par 
\par See also\tab \uldb \b Properties of Micron Marker\plain\b\fs24 {\v Properties_of_Micron_Marker}\plain\fs24 
