\pard\keepn \b\fs36\cf1 Mouse Control
\par \pard\tx355 \plain\fs24 
\par \{bmc bm65.bmp\} \tab \ul Clicking\plain\fs24 {\v CLICK@Sem.HLP} on this icon selects the \uldb \b Mouse Control Mode\plain\b\fs24 {\v Mouse_Control_Mode}\plain\fs24 , the Annotation Mode is disabled.
\par 
\par The mouse has special functions while it is in the \uldb \b Image Window\plain\b\fs24 {\v GIRNF0@Sem.HLP}\plain\fs24  and the Image Window Adjustment Mode is selected.
\par It  is not related to the current \uldb \b SEM Operating Mode\plain\b\fs24 {\v SEM_Operating_Mode}.
\par 
\par \{bmc bm7.bmp\} \tab \plain\fs24 Clicking on this icon selects the Annotation\b  \uldb Select Mode\plain\b\fs24 {\v Select_Mode}\plain\fs24 , the Mouse Control Mode is disabled.
\par \pard\tx355 
\par The left and right mouse buttons are used differently if the \b Annotation Mode\plain\fs24  is selected:
\par 
\par 
\par \{bmc bm10.bmp\}\tab \uldb \b selects\plain\b\fs24 {\v Object_Selection}\plain\fs24  annotation and measurement functions from the Annotation Panel. 
\par 
\par Clicking on the Image Window selects the place for Parameter, imported bitmaps, and Text annotation if one of the modes is selected.
\par 
\par Clicking on an annotation object selects it. Holding down \b <SHIFT>\plain\fs24  or \b <CTRL>\plain\fs24  allows to select many objects as you click on them. Drawing a frame around objects selects them.
\par \pard\tx355 
\par \{bmc bm8.bmp\}\tab Click on the Image Window with the right mouse button selects the \uldb \b Configuring Annotation\plain\b\fs24 {\v Configuring_Annotation}\plain\fs24  mode.
\par 
\par \{bmc bm95.bmp\}\tab The middle mouse button always adjusts the right parameter of the image window adjustment mode which is the yellow marked field in the \uldb \b Status Bar\plain\b\fs24 {\v RDJHU5@Sem.HLP}\plain\fs24 .
\par 
\par \page
