\pard\keepn \b\fs36\cf1 Object Selection
\par \pard \plain\fs24 
\par This mode operates when the current Image Manager mode is set to \uldb \b Select Mode\plain\b\fs24 {\v Select_Mode}\plain\fs24 . All selected objects are highlighted by selection \ul handles\plain\fs24 {\v Handles@Sem.HLP}, which identifies that they can either be moved, sized or ordered. Some objects have special behavior when double \ul clicked\plain\fs24 {\v CLICK@Sem.HLP}. 
\par 
\par When right clicking on an object a \uldb \b Popup Menu\plain\b\fs24 {\v Configuring_Annotation}\plain\fs24  may be displayed so that the \uldb \b properties of the object\plain\b\fs24 {\v Object_Properties}\plain\fs24  can be changed. If an object cannot be selected, then Image Manger may be in Mouse Control Mode, or the object may not be a selectable object (for example, \uldb \b Freeze Marker Objects\plain\b\fs24 {\v Freeze_Marker_Objects}\plain\fs24 ).
\par \pard 
\par \{bmc bm4.bmp\} Note that some objects such as the \uldb \b Reduced Raster\plain\b\fs24 {\v Reduced_Raster_Object}\plain\fs24  object may be selected both in \uldb \b Select Mode\plain\b\fs24 {\v Select_Mode}\plain\fs24  or in \uldb \b Mouse Control Mode\plain\b\fs24 {\v Mouse_Control_Mode}\plain\fs24 .
\par 
\par You may need to create one or two object to experiment with Object Selection Mode.
\par 
\par See also \uldb \b Simple Object Selection\plain\b\fs24 {\v Simple_Object_Selection} \plain\fs24 and \b  \uldb Multiple Object Selection\plain\b\fs24 {\v Multiple_Object_Selection}\plain\fs24 
\par \page
