\pard\keepn \b\fs36\cf1 Photo Development Timer
\par \pard \plain\fs24\cf2 The development timer is an easy way to measure the development time of a micrograph, it is simply a counter which will count down from a preset value to zero, at which point a \b 'beep'\plain\fs24\cf2  will be emitted.\plain\fs24 
\par \trowd\trgaph105\trleft-116 \cellx6765\cellx9855\pard\intbl\li355\fi-355\tx355 \cf2 \{bmc bm1.bmp\}\plain\fs24 \tab Start t\cf2 he timer by clicking on \b Start Development Timer\plain\fs24\cf2  .
\par\intbl 
\par\intbl \{bmc bm1.bmp\}\tab Clicking on the \b counter\plain\fs24\cf2  field allows the starting value to be entered (in seconds). The display is in minutes while the value is greater than 60 seconds, then in seconds down to zero. The maximum timer value is 300 seconds.\cell\pard \pard\intbl\li355\fi-355\tx355 \pard\intbl \{bmc bm100.bmp\}\cell\intbl\row
\pard 
