{\up $}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up $} Point to Point}
{\up #}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up #} 14_OZWO}
{\up >}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up >} main}
\pard\keepn \b\fs36\cf1 \{bmc bm89.bmp\}  Point to Point
\par \pard \plain\fs24 
\par This measurement facility comprises a related pair of markers, a \b reference marker\plain\fs24  (identified by the symbol \b PaRn\plain\fs24  ) and a \b measurement marker\plain\fs24  (identified by \b Pan\plain\fs24 )\b .\plain\fs24  Each marker may be adjusted in position. \uldb \b Precision Adjustment\plain\b\fs24 {\v Precision_Adjustment}\plain\fs24  is available
\par 
\par \trowd\trgaph105\trleft-116 \cellx7935\cellx12685\pard\intbl\li355\fi-355\tx355 \b \{bmc bm1.bmp\}\tab \plain\ul\fs24 Click\plain\fs24 {\v CLICK@Sem.HLP} on the \b Point to Point Icon \plain\fs24 to switch the function on or load it from the \uldb \b Menu Bar\plain\b\fs24 {\v 8ZP0K4@Sem.HLP}\plain\fs24 
\par\intbl 
\par\intbl \b \{bmc bm1.bmp\}\plain\fs24 \tab Point to the \b Zone\plain\fs24  for which you want to place the Point to Point Marker and click.
\par\intbl 
\par\intbl \b \{bmc bm1.bmp\}\plain\fs24 \tab Pick the \ul handle\plain\fs24 {\v Handles@Sem.HLP} of the \b Reference Point PaRn\plain\fs24  and place it.
\par\intbl 
\par\intbl \b \{bmc bm1.bmp\}\plain\fs24 \tab Pick the handle of the \b Measurement Point Pan\plain\fs24  and place it.
\par\intbl 
\par\intbl \b \{bmc bm1.bmp\}\plain\fs24 \tab Pick the \b centre handle\plain\fs24  to place the complete line.
\par\intbl 
\par\intbl \b \{bmc bm1.bmp\}\plain\fs24 \tab The data from this objects \uldb results panel\plain\fs24 {\v Results_Panel_Parameters} can be copied to the clipboard for insertion into a speadsheet. This is achieved using the \uldb Annotation Copy\plain\fs24 {\v Anntotation_to_Clipboard} Popup Menu item.
\par\intbl \cell\pard \pard\intbl\li355\fi-355\tx355 \pard\intbl \{bmc bm103.bmp\}\cell\intbl\row
\pard\li355\fi-355\tx355 \b \{bmc bm1.bmp\}\plain\fs24 \tab Double clicking on one of the markers calls the \uldb \b Results Panel\plain\b\fs24 {\v Results_Panel_Parameters}\plain\fs24  containing the measurement parameters which are:
\par \b \tab Pan \plain\fs24 Distance between the markers, 
\par \tab \b Pbn \plain\fs24 Angle between the line joining the markers and the direction of scan 
\par \tab where \b n\plain\fs24  is the instance identifier (i.e. 0 for first object created, 1 for second object up to 10 objects)
\par 
\par \b \{bmc bm1.bmp\}\plain\fs24 \tab When no measurement results are selected for display, the point to point marker displays the line length by the centre point on the line. Double clicking on this value allows a manual line length to be entered.
\par \pard\li355\fi-355\tx355 
\par \pard\tx355 \{bmc bm3.bmp\}\tab The dimensional measurement is derived from the zone magnification hence when multiple zones are present both markers must lie in the same zone. If the markers are moved into different zones the dimensional value is set to zero and a \b ? \plain\fs24 is annotated.
\par 
\par \pard\li355\fi-355\tx355 See also \uldb \b Retrospective Measurement\plain\b\fs24 {\v Retrospective_Measurement}\plain\fs24 . \tab \tab \uldb \b Properties of Point to Point Measurement\plain\b\fs24 {\v Properties_of_Point_to_Point_Measurement}\plain\fs24 
\par \page
{\up $}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up $} Precision Adjustment}
{\up #}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up #} Precision_Adjustment}
{\up >}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up >} main}
\pard\keepn \b\fs36\cf1 Precision Adjustment
\par \pard \plain\fs24 
\par \pard\li355\fi-355\tx355 \{bmc bm10.bmp\}\tab Although using the mouse is a very good method of moving quickly over the whole of the image it is not the best for precision adjustments as this would require a steady hand and in some circumstances the cursor obscures the point of interest.
\par \pard\tx355 
\par \pard\li355\fi-355\tx355 \{bmc bm28.bmp\}\tab In this case the arrow keys on the keyboard \{bmc bm73.bmp\}\{bmc bm75.bmp\}\{bmc bm74.bmp\}\{bmc bm76.bmp\}may be used to increment the position of a measurement object, or one of its \ul handles\plain\fs24 {\v Handles@Sem.HLP} Once an arrow key is used the mouse position is ignored (and hence the cursor may be moved out of the way). Press the \b Spacebar\plain\fs24  to select a different handle, the currently selected handle is highlighted in red. When no handles are selected, the cursor keys can then be used to move the whole object, rather than just a selected handle.
\par \pard\li355\fi-355\tx355 
\par \{bmc bm4.bmp\}\tab \tab \b <CTRL + Cursor>\plain\fs24  gives coarse adjustment. The \i Height\plain\fs24  and \i Width\plain\fs24  increments for coarse adjustment are defined by the \uldb Grid Settings Dialog\plain\fs24 {\v The_Snap_to_Grid_Option}. These settings are used regardless of the snap-to-grid function.
\par \page
{\up $}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up $} Print Setup Dialog}
{\up #}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up #} Print_Setup_Dialog}
\pard\keepn \b\fs36\cf1 Print Setup Dialog
\par \pard\tx355 \plain\fs24 This dialog is accessed through
\par \{bmc bm27.bmp\}\tab \b Menu File\plain\fs24 , \b Print Setup
\par 
\par \plain\fs24 or through
\par \b \{bmc bm8.bmp\}\plain\fs24 \tab right mouse button on the Image Window with \b Send To\plain\fs24  and \b Printer\plain\fs24 . 
\par When the \b Print Setup\plain\fs24  panel is displayed the operator is able to define how an image is being printed, i.e. whether to include annotation, overlay and color with the image and to what area of the page the image should be printed.
\par \trowd\trgaph105\trleft-116 \cellx7195\cellx14215\pard\intbl\tx355 Select \{bmc bm32.bmp\} the items to \ul merge\plain\fs24 {\v merge_settings} in the print If annotation is included see \ul Annotation Warning\plain\fs24 {\v Annotation_Warning}
\par\intbl 
\par\intbl In \b Size\plain\fs24  select\b  Fit to Page\plain\fs24  to adjust the print size to the page width or select\b  Zoom\plain\fs24  and from the Drop-down List one of the factors. The magnification of the printed image is indicated.
\par\intbl 
\par\intbl The \b Position\plain\fs24  of the print on the page can be selected to \b Top\plain\fs24 , \b Middle\plain\fs24  and \b Bottom \plain\fs24 by clicking on a Radio Button.
\par\intbl See also\b  \uldb Magnification Reference\plain\b\fs24 {\v 32AVUYD@leoserv.hlp}\plain\fs24  and \uldb \b Print No.\plain\b\fs24 {\v Print_No.}\plain\fs24 
\par\intbl \{bmc bm31.bmp\}\b \tab Before you start printing make sure, all settings of the printer (page layout etc.) are correct. (use \uldb Printer\plain\b\fs24 {\v Standard_Printer_dialog}\plain\fs24 )\cell\pard \pard\intbl\tx355 \{bmc bm104.bmp\}\cell\intbl\row
\pard\tx355 \b Print\plain\fs24  starts the printout of the image.
\par \pard\tx355 \b Close\plain\fs24  closes the setup dialog and preserves the settings you just made.
\par \pard\tx355 \b Cancel\plain\fs24  or clicking on \{bmc bm24.bmp\} closes the setup dialog and omits any changes made during this session.
\par \pard\tx355 \b Help\plain\fs24  calls this page.
\par \page
