{\up >}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up >} main}
\pard\keepn\tx355 \fs36\cf1 \{bmc bm90.bmp\}  Radial Measurement
\par \pard\tx355 \plain\fs24 
\par \pard\tx355 The radial measurement facility is a circle which may be adjusted in diameter \b Da n\plain\fs24 . \uldb \b Precision Adjustment\plain\b\fs24 {\v Precision_Adjustment}\plain\fs24  is available
\par \pard\tx355 
\par \trowd\trgaph105\trleft-116 \cellx9065\cellx11555\pard\intbl\li355\fi-355\tx355 \b \{bmc bm1.bmp\}\tab \plain\ul\fs24 Click\plain\fs24 {\v CLICK@Sem.HLP} on the \b Radial Measurement Icon \plain\fs24 to switch the function on.
\par\intbl 
\par\intbl \b \{bmc bm1.bmp\}\plain\fs24 \tab Point to the \uldb \b Zone\plain\b\fs24 {\v Zone}\plain\fs24  for which you want to place the Radial Measurement and click.
\par\intbl 
\par\intbl \b \{bmc bm1.bmp\}\plain\fs24 \tab Pick the \ul handles\plain\fs24 {\v Handles@Sem.HLP} of the \b Circle Da n\plain\fs24  and place them.
\par\intbl 
\par\intbl \{bmc bm1.bmp\}\tab Double clicking on the circle calls the \uldb \b Results Panel\plain\b\fs24 {\v Results_Panel_Parameters}\plain\fs24   containing the measurement parameter \b Da n \plain\fs24 the diameter of the circle where \b n\plain\fs24  is the instance identifier (i.e. 1 for first object created, 2 for second object) and \b Db n \plain\fs24 the area of the Circle
\par\intbl 
\par\intbl \b \{bmc bm1.bmp\}\plain\fs24 \tab The data from this objects \uldb results panel\plain\fs24 {\v Results_Panel_Parameters} can be copied to the clipboard for insertion into a speadsheet. This is achieved using the \uldb Annotation Copy\plain\fs24 {\v Anntotation_to_Clipboard} Popup Menu item.
\par\intbl \cell\pard \pard\intbl\li355\fi-355\tx355 \pard\intbl\tx355 \par\pard \pard\intbl \{bmc bm105.bmp\}\cell\intbl\row
\pard\li355\fi-355\tx355 
\par \pard\tx355 \{bmc bm3.bmp\}\tab The dimensional measurement is derived from the zone magnification hence when multiple zones are present the bounding square must wholly lie within a zone. If the bounding square is moved so that is spans zones the dimensional value is set to zero and a \b ? \plain\fs24 is annotated.
\par 
\par \pard\li355\fi-355\tx355 See also \uldb \b Retrospective Measurement\plain\b\fs24 {\v Retrospective_Measurement}\plain\fs24 . \tab \tab \uldb \b Properties of Radial Measurement\plain\b\fs24 {\v Properties_of_Radial_Measurement}\plain\fs24 
