{\up $}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up $} SEM Operating Mode}
{\up #}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up #} SEM_Operating_Mode}
{\up >}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up >} main}
\pard\keepn \b\fs36\cf1 SEM Operating Mode
\par \pard \plain\fs24 
\par This mode determines the format of the \uldb \b Image Window\plain\b\fs24 {\v GIRNF0@Sem.HLP}\plain\fs24 , and the format in which Image Data is scanned into the SEM Image Store, and is not related to the current\uldb \b  Image Manager Operating Mode\plain\b\fs24 {\v Mouse_Control}\plain\fs24 .
\par 
\par Depending on the SEM Operating Mode, the display may divided up into a number of \uldb \b Zones\plain\b\fs24 {\v Zone}\plain\fs24 .
\par 
\par The following objects may be available for selection, however certain \uldb \b Licences\plain\b\fs24 {\v Reasons_for_missing_greyed_Functions}\plain\fs24  may be required to enter particular modes :
\par \pard 
\par \pard\tx355 \tab \uldb \b Reduced Raster Object\plain\b\fs24 {\v Reduced_Raster_Object}\plain\fs24 
\par 
\par \tab \uldb \b Split Screen Object\plain\b\fs24 {\v Split_Screen_Object}\plain\fs24 
\par 
