{\up $}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up $} Save User Settings}
{\up #}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up #} Save_User_Settings}
{\up >}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up >} main}
\pard\keepn\tx355 \b\fs36\cf1 Save User Settings
\par \pard\tx355 \plain\fs24 
\par \pard\tx355 User settings may be saved on disk and \uldb \b loaded back again\plain\b\fs24 {\v Load_User_Settings}\plain\fs24  for later use. The are saved in the user directory by default and have the extension \b *.anp\plain\fs24 . The default file for current annotation preferences is \uldb \b CURRENT.ANP\plain\b\fs24 {\v User_Preferences_File}\plain\fs24  
\par \pard\tx355 \b 
\par \pard\tx355 \plain\fs24 Dialogs guide you through the procedure.
\par \pard\tx355 
\par \trowd\trgaph105\trleft-116 \cellx6795\cellx13815\pard\intbl\li355\fi-355\tx355 \b \{bmc bm1.bmp\}\plain\fs24 \tab If you are not in your \b User Directory\plain\fs24  as shown in the 
\par\intbl \b \tab Look In\plain\fs24  box use \{bmc bm69.bmp\} button to navigate to your directory.
\par\intbl 
\par\intbl \b \{bmc bm1.bmp\}\plain\fs24 \tab Select \b User Preferences\plain\fs24  from the \b Files of Type\plain\fs24  \ul Drop-down List\plain\fs24 {\v XYVXW3@Sem.HLP} box.
\par\intbl 
\par\intbl \b \{bmc bm1.bmp\}\plain\fs24 \tab Enter the file name (e.g. User1.anp) into the \b File Name\plain\fs24  box.
\par\intbl 
\par\intbl \b \{bmc bm1.bmp\}\plain\fs24 \tab Click on the \b OK\plain\fs24  button to save the file.
\par\intbl 
\par\intbl \b \{bmc bm1.bmp\}\plain\fs24 \tab Click on the \b Cancel\plain\fs24  button if you don't want to save the file.\cell\pard \pard\intbl\li355\fi-355\tx355 \pard\intbl \{bmc bm114.bmp\}\cell\intbl\row
\pard 
