{\up $}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up $} Saving Annotation}
{\up #}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up #} 4G4W_J6}
{\up >}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up >} main}
\pard\keepn \b\fs36\cf1 \{bmc bm115.bmp\}  Saving Annotation
\par \pard \plain\fs24 
\par This function is used to save Annotation Data to file.
\par 
\par \trowd\trgaph105\trleft-116 \cellx4535\cellx13535\pard\intbl\li355\fi-355\tx355 \{bmc bm10.bmp\}\tab \ul Clicking\plain\fs24 {\v CLICK@Sem.HLP} on the \b Save Annotation\plain\fs24  icon calls a standard Save File Dialog.\par\pard \pard\intbl\tx355 \par\pard \pard\intbl\tx355 Annotation files are saved by default to the User Directory and have the extension \b *.ANN.\par\pard \pard\intbl\tx355 \plain\fs24 \par\pard \pard\intbl\li355\fi-355\tx355 \b \{bmc bm1.bmp\}\tab \plain\fs24 You are prompted to enter a \b file name.\par\pard \pard\intbl\tx355 \plain\fs24 If a filename is already present you are asked whether or not the present file should be overwritten with the file to be saved.\par\pard \pard\intbl\tx355 \b \par\pard \pard\intbl\li355\fi-355\tx355 \plain\fs24 \{bmc bm4.bmp\} Note that two file types are supported by this dialog \b .ANN \plain\fs24 (annotation) and \b .ADZ\plain\fs24  (annotation data zone).\cell\pard \pard\intbl\li355\fi-355\tx355 \pard\intbl\tx355 \par\pard \pard\intbl \{bmc bm116.bmp\}\cell\intbl\row
\pard 
\par \{bmc bm31.bmp\}The \b Save Selected Annotation Only\plain\fs24  check box on the dialog is useful when only \uldb \b selected\plain\b\fs24 {\v Object_Selection}\plain\fs24  annotation objects, need to be saved. This is especially useful when saving \uldb \b Sticky Panel Objects\plain\b\fs24 {\v Sticky_Panel_Annotation}\plain\fs24  for example into \b .ADZ\plain\fs24  files to later be loaded as \uldb \b data zones\plain\b\fs24 {\v Data_Zone}\plain\fs24 .
\par \page
