\par 
\par \page
{\up $}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up $} Select Buttons}
{\up #}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up #} Select_Buttons}
{\up >}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up >} main}
\pard\keepn\tx355 \b\fs36\cf1 Select Buttons
\par \pard\tx355 \plain\fs24 
\par \pard\tx355 \b\fs28 Enter Select Mode on New Object:
\par \pard\tx355 \plain\fs24 In this mode you return to the selection mode after you have created an object. Selection mode selects the object (\ul handles\plain\fs24 {\v Handles@Leo_1500.HLP} appear) for further adjustment and alignment.
\par \pard\tx355 
\par \pard\tx355 \b\fs28 Keep Current Tool Button Selected:
\par \pard\tx355 \plain\fs24 In this mode the tool button is kept selected. So each time you click in the Image Window an new object of the same type is generated up to the maximum number of objects on the overlay plane (usually 2).
\par \pard\tx355 
\par \pard\li355\fi-355\tx355 The selected mode is checked with \{bmc bm23.bmp\}.
\par \pard\tx355 
\par \page
{\up $}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up $} Select Mode}
{\up #}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up #} Select_Mode}
{\up >}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up >} main}
\pard\keepn \b\fs36\cf1 \{bmc bm7.bmp\}  Select Mode
\par \pard \plain\fs24 
\par In this mode, the user can \uldb \b select objects\plain\b\fs24 {\v Object_Selection}\plain\fs24 , or groups of objects for moving or deletion. If an individual object is selected then it can also be sized. 
\par 
\par \pard\li355\fi-355\tx355 \{bmc bm4.bmp\} Note that if parameters are assigned for mouse adjustment (See \uldb \b Status Bar Parameter Control\plain\b\fs24 {\v T3KQVM@Sem.HLP}\plain\fs24 ), no adjustment will be performed while Image Manager is in this mode.
\par \pard\tx355 
\par \pard\tx355 With the \uldb \b Annotation Toolbar\plain\b\fs24 {\v Calling_the_Annotation_Toolbar}\plain\fs24  displayed, this is the default mode. The opposite of select mode is \uldb \b Mouse Control Mode\plain\b\fs24 {\v Mouse_Control_Mode}\plain\fs24 . In Mouse Control Mode, the Image Manager acts as if the toolbar were not being displayed, and ignores all object selections that could otherwise be made if Select Mode were active.
\par \pard\tx355 
\par \pard\tx355 This mode also affects the \uldb \b Context Sensitive Popup Menu\plain\b\fs24 {\v Context_Sensitive_Popup_Menu}\plain\fs24 .
\par \pard\tx355 
\par \pard\tx355 See also \uldb \b Mouse Control\plain\b\fs24 {\v Mouse_Control}\plain\fs24 
\par \page
