{\up $}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up $} Standard Measurement System}
{\up #}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up #} Standard_Measurement_System}
{\up >}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up >} main}
\pard\keepn \b\fs36\cf1 Standard Measurement System
\par \pard \plain\fs24 
\par The angles used in measurement are, 0\'b0-360\'b0, with 0\'b0 being measured perpendicular to the SEM Raster Scan line, traveling clockwise to 360\'b0. 
\par 
\par Other measurement values have a base unit of metres, but are automatically formatted to engineering units where appropriate (mm, \'b5m, nm). This formatting depends on the current value of Pixel Size, which in turn is dependent on the \uldb \b Zone\plain\b\fs24 {\v Zone}\plain\fs24  that the object is in, and the magnification factor that is being applied to the zone when the measurement object is being displayed.
\par \page
