\par \trowd\trgaph105\trleft-116 \cellx6795\cellx13815\pard\intbl\li355\fi-355\tx355 \{bmc bm1.bmp\}\tab Select the printer type on which you want to print the image from the \b Name\plain\fs24  Drop-down List. \par\pard \pard\intbl\tx355 \par\pard \pard\intbl\tx355 \b Status\plain\fs24  (of the printer like Ready), \b Type\plain\fs24  (of the printer like HP LaserJet 4V) and \b Where\plain\fs24  (the path to the printer) give you additional information.\par\pard \pard\intbl\tx355 \par\pard \pard\intbl\li355\fi-355\tx355 \{bmc bm1.bmp\}\tab With \b Properties \plain\fs24 you select and set the parameters of the printer in use.\par\pard \pard\intbl\tx355 \par\pard \pard\intbl\li355\fi-355\tx355 \{bmc bm1.bmp\}\tab You may print the image to a print file for later printing if you check \{bmc bm32.bmp\} \b Print to file\plain\fs24 . \par\pard \pard\intbl\tx355 \par\pard \pard\intbl\li355\fi-355\tx355 \{bmc bm1.bmp\}\b \tab Print range \plain\fs24 is generally All because you print 1 image at a time from the SEM application.\par\pard \pard\intbl\tx355 \par\pard \pard\intbl\li355\fi-355\tx355 \{bmc bm1.bmp\}\tab In \b Copies\plain\fs24  select the number of copies with the scroll bar or type the parameter into the filed.\cell\pard \pard\intbl\li355\fi-355\tx355 \pard\intbl \{bmc bm125.bmp\}\cell\intbl\row
