{\up $}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up $} Sticky Panel Annotation}
{\up #}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up #} 1BX80Z0}
{\up >}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up >} main}
\pard\keepn \b\fs36\cf1 \{bmc bm19.bmp\}  Sticky Panel Annotation
\par \pard \plain\fs24 
\par Adds a rectangle to the overlay plane onto which annotation objects can be "stuck". The rectangle can be transparent or filled with a pattern. A transparent background can be achieved by setting the \uldb Brush Style\plain\fs24 {\v Selection_of_Brush_Settings} to Hollow, and the \uldb Pen Settings\plain\fs24 {\v Selection_of_Pen_Settings} to Invisible.
\par 
\par \trowd\trgaph105\trleft-116 \cellx7935\cellx12405\pard\intbl\li355\fi-355\tx355 \b \{bmc bm1.bmp\}\plain\fs24 \tab Select the \b Sticky Panel Annotation Icon\plain\fs24 .
\par\intbl 
\par\intbl \b \{bmc bm1.bmp\}\plain\fs24 \tab Point to the \b place\plain\fs24  where you want to start the rectangle and \ul drag\plain\fs24 {\v DRAG@Sem.HLP} to the place where you want to end the rectangle.
\par\intbl 
\par\intbl \b \{bmc bm1.bmp\}\plain\fs24 \tab The rectangle will be shown at the selected place of the Image Window and can be dragged into the required \b position\plain\fs24 .\cell\pard \pard\intbl\li355\fi-355\tx355 \pard\intbl\tx355 \par\pard \pard\intbl\tx355 \par\pard \pard\intbl\tx355 \{bmc bm127.bmp\}\par\pard \pard\intbl \cell\intbl\row
\pard\li355\fi-355\tx355 \b \{bmc bm1.bmp\}\plain\fs24 \tab \{bmc bm31.bmp\} The \ul handles\plain\fs24 {\v Handles@Sem.HLP} of the rectangle can be clicked on and used for resizing the rectangle. Holding down \b <SHIFT>\plain\fs24  while dragging the mouse will proportionally scale all objects inside the panel, along with the panel itself.
\par 
\par \b \{bmc bm1.bmp\}\plain\fs24 \tab To "stick" objects to a panel, simply click and drag them over the panel when in \uldb Selection Mode\plain\fs24 {\v Select_Mode}. When releasing the left mouse button, the top left corner of the object being "stuck" to the panel must be anywhere within the bounds of the panel rectangle.
\par \pard\li355\fi-355\tx355 
\par The coordinates of the rectangle are displayed in the \uldb Status Bar\plain\fs24 {\v RDJHU5@Sem.HLP}. \{bmc bm128.bmp\}
\par (From corner X/Y to opposite corner X/Y, centre X/Y, size X/Y)
\par \pard\tx355 
\par \pard\tx355 See also\tab \b  \uldb Properties of Sticky Panel Annotation\plain\b\fs24 {\v Properties_of_Sticky_Panel_Annotation}\plain\fs24 
\par \pard\li355\fi-355\tx355 
\par \page
