{\up $}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up $} Sticky Panel Lock Property}
{\up #}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up #} Sticky_Panel_Lock_Property}
{\up >}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up >} main}
\pard\keepn \b\fs36\cf1 Sticky Panel Lock Property
\par \pard \plain\fs24 
\par This property only applies to \uldb \b Sticky Panel Objects\plain\b\fs24 {\v Sticky_Panel_Annotation}\plain\fs24 . 
\par 
\par When this flag is set, any objects that are 'stuck' to this panel cannot be \uldb \b selected\plain\b\fs24 {\v Object_Selection}\plain\fs24  or otherwise edited. This prevents accidental activation of objects when moving or sizing sticky panel objects. 
\par 
\par The exception to this rule is that double \ul clicking\plain\fs24 {\v CLICK@Sem.HLP} of objects is still valid, this is especially useful for example if
\par a \uldb \b SEM Parameter Object\plain\b\fs24 {\v SEM_Parameter_Object}\plain\fs24  is stuck to a panel. When the parameter object is double clicked in \uldb \b Mouse Control Mode\plain\b\fs24 {\v Mouse_Control_Mode}\plain\fs24 , a user input box appears with the option to adjust the selected parameter.
\par \page
