{\up $}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up $} Stored Data Histogram}
{\up #}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up #} Stored_Data_Histogram}
{\up >}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up >} main}
\pard\keepn\tx355 \b\fs36\cf1 \{bmc bm93.bmp\}  Stored Data Histogram
\par \pard\tx355 \plain\fs24 
\par \pard\tx355 The histogram function displays a histogram of the stored image.
\par \pard\tx355 
\par \trowd\trqc\trgaph109\trleft-111 \cellx7944\cellx13543\pard\intbl\li355\fi-355\tx355 
\par\intbl \b \{bmc bm1.bmp\}\plain\fs24 \tab \ul Click\plain\fs24 {\v CLICK@Sem.HLP} on the \b Stored Data Histogram Icon \plain\fs24 to switch to histogram creation mode.
\par\intbl 
\par\intbl \b \{bmc bm1.bmp\}\plain\fs24 \tab \b Click on the image\plain\fs24  on the area in the which you want the top left corner of the histogram to be displayed. The histogram will auto-scale itself to a default width and height
\par\intbl 
\par\intbl \b \{bmc bm1.bmp\}\plain\fs24 \tab The histogram will be shown at the selected position in the Image Window, and can be \ul dragged\plain\fs24 {\v DRAG@Sem.HLP} to a new \b position\plain\fs24  as required.
\par\intbl \cell\pard \pard\intbl\li355\fi-355\tx355 \pard\intbl \{bmc bm129.bmp\}\cell\intbl\row
\pard\li355\fi-355\tx355 \b \{bmc bm1.bmp\}\plain\fs24 \tab Using the \ul handles\plain\fs24 {\v Handles@Sem.HLP} the histogram can also be sized.
\par 
\par \b \{bmc bm1.bmp\}\plain\fs24 \tab Note that the histogram bin cursors at bin positions 34 and 103 can be clicked and dragged to highlight the desired bin number. Holding the \b Shift\plain\fs24  key whilst dragging one cursor, moves the other cursor by the same amount. 
\par 
\par \b \{bmc bm1.bmp\}\plain\fs24 \tab The data for the histogram can be copied to the clipboard for insertion into a speadsheet. This is achieved using the \uldb Annotation Copy\plain\fs24 {\v Anntotation_to_Clipboard} Popup Menu item.
\par \pard\li355\fi-355\tx355 
\par See also\tab  \uldb \b Properties of Stored Data Histogram\plain\b\fs24 {\v Properties_of_Stored_Data_Histogram}\plain\fs24 
\par \page
{\up $}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up $} Stored Vector Profile}
{\up #}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up #} Stored_Vector_Profile}
{\up >}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up >} main}
\pard\keepn \b\fs36\cf1 \{bmc bm92.bmp\}  Stored Vector Profile
\par \pard \plain\fs24 
\par The Stored Vector Profile function brings up the profile display along a measurement line on the stored image.
\par \uldb \b Precision Adjustment\plain\b\fs24 {\v Precision_Adjustment}\plain\fs24  is available.
\par 
\par \trowd\trqc\trgaph109\trleft-111 \cellx7944\cellx12414\pard\intbl\li355\fi-355\tx355 \b \{bmc bm1.bmp\}\plain\fs24 \tab \ul Click\plain\fs24 {\v CLICK@Sem.HLP} on the \b Stored Vector Profile Icon \plain\fs24 to switch the function on.
\par\intbl 
\par\intbl \b \{bmc bm1.bmp\}\plain\fs24 \tab \b Draw a line\plain\fs24  for which you want to show the grey level profile.
\par\intbl 
\par\intbl \b \{bmc bm1.bmp\}\plain\fs24 \tab This line may be moved on the stored image of the Image Window and can be \ul dragged\plain\fs24 {\v DRAG@Sem.HLP} into the required \b position\plain\fs24 .
\par\intbl \tab Using the \ul handles\plain\fs24 {\v Handles@Sem.HLP} the line can also be sized.
\par\intbl 
\par\intbl \b \{bmc bm1.bmp\}\plain\fs24 \tab When the line is dropped the trace on the \b profile display\plain\fs24  describes the grey levels lying under the line. Note that the leftmost point of the line is the leftmost position on the profile display. The display can be dragged to size.
\par\intbl 
\par\intbl \b \{bmc bm1.bmp\}\plain\fs24 \tab Note that the profile width cursors can be clicked and dragged to highlight the desired profile position. Holding the \b Shift\plain\fs24  key whilst dragging one cursor, moves the other cursor by the same amount. 
\par\intbl \cell\pard \pard\intbl\li355\fi-355\tx355 \pard\intbl \{bmc bm130.bmp\}\cell\intbl\row
\pard\li355\fi-355\tx355 \b \{bmc bm1.bmp\}\plain\fs24 \tab Note also that an alternative to dragging the cursors is to adjust the cursor markers actualy on the profile line itself. This allows for accurate feature alignment. Click and drag these markers to adjust the profile cursors.
\par 
\par \b \{bmc bm1.bmp\}\plain\fs24 \tab If not already displayed, double click on the profile to open the \uldb \b Results Panel\plain\b\fs24 {\v Results_Panel_Parameters}\plain\fs24  and add the \b Profile Width\plain\fs24  parameter which shows the distance between the cursors in the profile plot. 
\par 
\par \b \{bmc bm1.bmp\}\plain\fs24 \tab The data from this objects \uldb results panel\plain\fs24 {\v Results_Panel_Parameters} can be copied to the clipboard for insertion into a speadsheet. This is achieved using the \uldb Annotation Copy\plain\fs24 {\v Anntotation_to_Clipboard} Popup Menu item.
\par \pard\li355\fi-355\tx355 
\par \{bmc bm4.bmp\}Changing the magnification setting on the microscope will invalidate the profile graph, as the object no longer represents the data that was previously sampled and stored. In this case, double click on the profile graphic to resample the profile data.
\par 
\par \{bmc bm3.bmp\} The dimensional measurement is derived from the zone magnification hence when multiple zones are present both markers must lie in the same zone. If the markers are moved into different zones the dimensional value is set to zero and a \b ? \plain\fs24 is annotated.
\par \pard\tx355 
\par \pard\tx355 See also\tab  \uldb \b Properties of Stored Vector Profile\plain\b\fs24 {\v Properties_of_Stored_Vector_Profile}\plain\fs24 
\par \page
{\up $}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up $} TIFF Data Annotation}
{\up #}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up #} 361T0QU}
{\up >}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up >} main}
\pard\keepn\tx355 \b\fs36\cf1 \{bmc bm20.bmp\}  TIFF Data Annotation
\par \pard\tx355 \plain\fs24 
\par \pard\tx355 This function creates a sequence of annotation objects which contain data from the currently loaded TIFF file which were saved as User \uldb Selected Parameters\plain\fs24 {\v Export_Tiff_Data}.
\par \pard\tx355 
\par \trowd\trgaph105\trleft-116 \cellx7935\cellx12965\pard\intbl\li355\fi-355\tx355 \b \{bmc bm1.bmp\}\plain\fs24 \tab Select the \b TIFF Data Icon\plain\fs24 .
\par\intbl \b \{bmc bm1.bmp\}\plain\fs24 \tab Point to the \b place\plain\fs24  where you want to start the annotation and \ul click\plain\fs24 {\v CLICK@Sem.HLP}.
\par\intbl \b \{bmc bm1.bmp\}\plain\fs24 \tab The \b Annotation SEM TIFF Parameter\plain\fs24  panel will appear.
\par\intbl \b \{bmc bm1.bmp\}\plain\fs24 \tab \b Mark\plain\fs24  the Parameter which you want to display. It shows in the top window.
\par\intbl \b \{bmc bm1.bmp\}\plain\fs24 \tab With \b <OK>\plain\fs24 .the parameter will be annotated. The procedure can be repeated.
\par\intbl \b \{bmc bm1.bmp\}\plain\fs24 \tab \b <Remove>\plain\fs24  removes a marked item from the list.
\par\intbl \b \{bmc bm1.bmp\}\plain\fs24 \tab \b <Remove All>\plain\fs24  clears the list after confirmation of a safety request input panel.
\par\intbl \b \{bmc bm1.bmp\}\plain\fs24 \tab \b <Cancel>\plain\fs24  or closing with \{bmc bm24.bmp\} leaves the Annotation box without transferring parameters.\cell\pard \pard\intbl\li355\fi-355\tx355 \pard\intbl\tx355 \{bmc bm131.bmp\}\par\pard \pard\intbl \cell\intbl\row
\pard\li355\fi-355\tx355 \b \{bmc bm1.bmp\}\plain\fs24 \tab The parameter(s) will be shown at the selected place of the image Window and can be dragged into the required \b position\plain\fs24 .
\par \b \{bmc bm1.bmp\}\plain\fs24 \tab If you have edited text (e.g. deleted) you can revert it with \b <Undo>\plain\fs24 .
\par 
\par \{bmc bm31.bmp\}\tab These TIFF data objects may be placed in a \uldb \b Sticky Panel\plain\b\fs24 {\v Sticky_Panel_Annotation}\plain\fs24  or User Defined \uldb \b Data Zone\plain\b\fs24 {\v Data_Zone}\plain\fs24 . They have the special property that when the datum is not available they display it as \b ?\plain\fs24 .
\par 
\par 
\par See also: \tab \tab \uldb \b Parameter Annotation\plain\b\fs24 {\v Parameter_Annotation} \tab \tab \uldb Properties of TIFF Data Annotation\plain\b\fs24 {\v Properties_of_TIFF_Data_Annotation}
\par \pard\li355\fi-355\tx355 
\par \tab \tab \tab \tab \uldb Retrospective Measurement\plain\b\fs24 {\v Retrospective_Measurement}\plain\fs24 
\par \page
