\pard\keepn \b\fs36\cf1 TIFF Import Object
\par \pard \plain\fs24 
\par 
\par \trowd\trgaph105\trleft-116 \cellx8495\cellx12965\pard\intbl Once created by the \uldb \b TIFF Import Dialog\plain\b\fs24 {\v Import_TIFF}\plain\fs24 , this object allows the area it defines on the \uldb \b Image Window\plain\b\fs24 {\v GIRNF0@Sem.HLP}\plain\fs24  to be used to Import Image Data from a TIFF File.
\par\intbl 
\par\intbl The \uldb \b selected\plain\b\fs24 {\v Object_Selection}\plain\fs24  object can be moved by \ul clicking\plain\fs24 {\v CLICK@Sem.HLP} inside the object and \ul dragging\plain\fs24 {\v DRAG@Sem.HLP} the mouse. 
\par\intbl 
\par\intbl Right clicking on the object displays its \uldb \b properties menu\plain\b\fs24 {\v Annotation_Settings}\plain\fs24 . From this menu, new object attributes or properties can be defined for this instance of the object.\cell\pard \pard\intbl \{bmc bm36.bmp\}\cell\intbl\row
\trowd\trgaph105\trleft-116 \cellx8495\cellx12965\pard\intbl This object is the opposite of a \uldb \b TIFF Export Objec\plain\b\fs24 {\v Export_TIFF}\plain\fs24 t. This object is automatically created if no existing Import Area Object is present when the user selects an Import function from either the \uldb \b Annotation Settings\plain\b\fs24 {\v Annotation_Settings}\plain\fs24  Popup-menu or from the \uldb \b Utility Popup Menu\plain\b\fs24 {\v Utility_Popup_Menu}\plain\fs24 , or even from its own properties menu as shown above.\cell\pard \pard\intbl \{bmc bm132.bmp\}\cell\intbl\row
\pard 
