{\up $}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up $} The Return to Select Mode Option}
{\up #}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up #} The_Return_to_Select_Mode_Option}
{\up >}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up >} main}
\pard\keepn \b\fs36\cf1 The Return to Select Mode Option
\par \pard \plain\fs24 
\par This option affects the functionality of the \uldb \b Annotation Toolbar\plain\b\fs24 {\v Calling_the_Annotation_Toolbar}\plain\fs24 . 
\par 
\par When this option is set, after performing an operation such as creating an annotation object, \uldb \b Select Mode\plain\b\fs24 {\v Select_Mode}\plain\fs24  is automatically entered and the toolbar Select Mode button is shown as pressed \{bmc bm7.bmp\}. This then allows further operations to be performed on the newly created object.
\par 
\par When this option is \b not\plain\fs24  set, the currently selected toolbar function remains active, and allows further instances of the same object to be created. 
\par \pard 
\par This may be useful when for example creating a set of \uldb \b Annotation Lines\plain\b\fs24 {\v Line_Annotation}\plain\fs24  for labeling a specimen, without having to select the Annotation Line toolbar button \{bmc bm16.bmp\} repeatedly.
\par 
\par This setting is automatically saved in the users directory into a \uldb \b CURRENT.ANP\plain\b\fs24 {\v User_Preferences_File}\plain\fs24  file.
\par \page
