\par 
\par This setting is automatically saved in the users directory into a \uldb \b CURRENT.ANP\plain\b\fs24 {\v User_Preferences_File}\plain\fs24 
\par \page
{\up $}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up $} The Snap to Grid Option}
\pard\keepn {\up #}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up #} The_Snap_to_Grid_Option}
\b\fs36\cf1 The Snap to Grid Option
\par \pard \plain\fs24 
\par The following dialog is displayed for the user to select the grid settings, and is accessed via 
\par the \uldb \b Annotation Settings Pop Up Menu\plain\b\fs24 {\v Annotation_Settings}\plain\fs24  :
\par 
\par \trowd\trgaph105\trleft-116 \cellx8495\cellx12115\pard\intbl When the\i  \plain\b\fs24 Snap to Grid\plain\fs24  option is checked \{bmc bm32.bmp\}, objects that this preference affects will only be able to be sized and moved over the \uldb \b Image Window\plain\b\fs24 {\v GIRNF0@Sem.HLP}\plain\fs24  to the accuracy given in the \b Width\plain\fs24  and \b Height\plain\fs24  input boxes. 
\par\intbl 
\par\intbl This option is useful for aligning \uldb \b text objects\plain\b\fs24 {\v Text_Annotation}\plain\fs24  for example. When displayed, the \uldb \b Annotation Toolbar\plain\b\fs24 {\v Calling_the_Annotation_Toolbar}\plain\fs24  will display an \b S\plain\fs24  in its title if the \b Snap to Grid\plain\fs24  setting is enabled.
\par\intbl 
\par\intbl These settings are automatically saved in the users directory into a \uldb \b CURRENT.ANP\plain\b\fs24 {\v User_Preferences_File}\plain\fs24  file.\cell\pard \pard\intbl \{bmc bm9.bmp\}\cell\intbl\row
\pard 
