\pard\keepn \b\fs36\cf1 The User Defaults or User Settings Option
\par \pard \plain\fs24 
\par When the Use Defaults Option is selected from the \uldb \b Annotation Settings Popup Menu\plain\b\fs24 {\v Annotation_Settings}\plain\fs24  , each object that is created will have a default set of properties such as line width and colour, or font size and colour. These defaults are defined by the system for the objects being created.
\par 
\par When the defaults option is not selected, then the User settings are used to define the properties of annotation objects that are subsequently created. These user settings are selected from the \uldb \b Context Sensitive Popup Menu\plain\b\fs24 {\v Context_Sensitive_Popup_Menu}\plain\fs24 , and are stored in the \uldb \b Users Preferences File\plain\b\fs24 {\v User_Preferences_File}\plain\fs24 . User perferences containing new settings can be saved or loaded, again by using the \uldb \b Load User Settings\plain\b\fs24 {\v Load_User_Settings}\plain\fs24  option from Image Manager Popup Menu.
\par \pard 
\par This setting is automatically saved in the users directory into a \uldb \b CURRENT.ANP\plain\b\fs24 {\v User_Preferences_File}\plain\fs24  file.
\par \page
