{\up $}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up $} Undo Last Edit}
{\up #}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up #} I48TXZ}
{\up >}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up >} main}
\pard\keepn \b\fs36\cf1 \{bmc bm44.bmp\}  Undo Last Edit
\par \pard\tx355 \plain\fs24 
\par \{bmc bm10.bmp\}\tab \ul Clicking\plain\fs24 {\v CLICK@Sem.HLP} on the \b Undo Last Edit\plain\fs24  icon reverts the last editing action, and then the icon is disabled (greyed).
\par 
\par \{bmc bm4.bmp\}\tab The icon is only active if a editing action was performed previously.
\par 
\par When an object has been \uldb \b created\plain\b\fs24 {\v Creation_of_Objects}\plain\fs24 , edited or moved, either by using the mouse or the \uldb \b keyboard\plain\b\fs24 {\v Keyboard_Adjustment}\plain\fs24 , the Image Manager takes a temporary 'snap-shot' of the current \i set\plain\fs24  of annotation objects.
\par 
\par When the undo function is called, the previous annotation \i set\plain\fs24  is re-instated.
\par \pard\tx355 
\par When the \uldb \b Annotation Toolbar\plain\b\fs24 {\v Calling_the_Annotation_Toolbar}\plain\fs24  button for this function is 'greyed' no undo action can be performed. Either the object being edited does not support an undo function, or the undo function has already been called / there is nothing to undo.
\par 
\par \pard\li355\fi-355\tx355 \{bmc bm4.bmp\} \b Note \plain\i\fs24 :\plain\fs24  This function does not undo SEM parameter value changes unless they are specific to a graphic object. For example, changing the angle of an \uldb \b Angular Measurement \plain\b\fs24 {\v Angular_Measurement}\plain\fs24 object will adjust the angular SEM parameter, performing an undo will reset the angle to that before the edit, and change the SEM parameter correspondingly.
\par \page
