{\up $}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up $} Unhide Annotation}
{\up #}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up #} 1OSL3AM}
{\up >}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up >} main}
\pard\keepn \b\fs36\cf1 Unhide Annotation
\par \pard \plain\fs24 
\par This function allows to unhide annotation objects which have been hidden before in a differentiated way:
\par 
\par \b\fs28 Unhide Selected Objects:
\par \plain\fs24 
\par \b\fs28 Unhide Standard Annotation:
\par \plain\fs24 Hidden standard annotation objects (text, parameter annotation, bitmap, line, rectangle, ellipse, sticky panel, TIFF data) become visible.
\par 
\par \b\fs28 Unhide Measurement Annotation:
\par \plain\fs24 Hidden measurement annotation objects (Micron Bars, Point to Point, Angular, Line Width, Circular, Horizontal, Vertical, Vector Profile) become visible.
\par \pard\tx355 
\par \b\fs28 Unhide Data Zone Annotation:
\par \plain\fs24 The hidden Data Zone becomes visible.
\par 
\par \b\fs28 Unhide Image Selection Area(s):
\par \plain\fs24 Hidden selected areas are set visible.
\par 
\par \b\fs28 Unhide Image Selection Handles:
\par \plain\fs24 Image Selection Handles are set visible.
\par 
\par \b\fs28 Unhide Results Panels:
\par \plain\fs24 Measurement Objects Results Panels are set visible.
\par 
\par \b\fs28 Unhide All:
\par \plain\fs24 Sets all of the above hidden annotation objects visible.
\par 
\par \{bmc bm28.bmp\}\tab The short cut from the keyboard is \b <CTRL + U>.\plain\fs24 
\par \page
