\pard \b\fs36\cf1 Zone
\par 
\par \plain\fs24 The \uldb \b Image Window\plain\b\fs24 {\v GIRNF0@Sem.HLP}\plain\fs24  can be divided up into a number of zones, depending on the currently selected \uldb \b SEM Operating Mode\plain\b\fs24 {\v SEM_Operating_Mode}\plain\fs24 .
\par 
\par When detectors are selected to particular zones, and the brightness and/or contrast of the image needs to be adjusted for example, by changing detector settings; there needs to be an easy way of telling the SEM which zone this adjustment applies to. The \uldb \b Zone Selection Marker\plain\b\fs24 {\v Zone_Selection_Marker}\plain\fs24  is used to achieve this.
\par \pard 
\par \page
