{\up $}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up $} Zone Selection Marker}
{\up #}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up #} Zone_Selection_Marker}
{\up >}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up >} main}
\pard\keepn\tx355 \b\fs36\cf1 Zone Selection Marker
\par \pard\tx355 \plain\fs24 
\par \pard\tx355 This object appears when there is more than one \uldb \b Zone\plain\b\fs24 {\v Zone}\plain\fs24  on the \uldb I\b mage Window\plain\b\fs24 {\v GIRNF0@Sem.HLP}\plain\fs24  such as in \uldb \b Split Screen Mode\plain\b\fs24 {\v Split_Screen_Object}\plain\fs24 . It appears as an \b anchor\plain\fs24  shaped object :
\par \pard\tx355 
\par \tab \{bmc bm121.bmp\}
\par 
\par The \b anchor\plain\fs24  shows in the currently selected zone.
\par 
\par Double clicking on the anchor graphic changes its appearance :
\par 
\par \tab \{bmc bm139.bmp\}
\par 
\par This denotes that \b all zones\plain\fs24 , are being controlled at once (e.g. adjustments to the detectors assigned to each zone are all applied at once, instead of to the detectors just assigned to the curently selected zone).
\par \page
{\up $}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up $} merge settings}
{\up #}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up #} merge_settings}
\pard\tx355 \b\fs36\cf1 Merge Settings
\par \pard\tx355 \plain\fs24 
\par \pard\tx355 These settings define what is to be merged with the image when saving it.
\par \pard\tx355 
\par \pard\tx355 Select \{bmc bm32.bmp\}\b Annotation\plain\fs24  to merge the annotation and measurement objects with the image.
\par \pard\tx355 
\par \pard\tx355 Select \{bmc bm32.bmp\}\b Overlay\plain\fs24  to merge the real time profile display with the image
\par \pard\tx355 
\par \pard\tx355 Select \{bmc bm32.bmp\}\b Colour Merge \plain\fs24 if you wish the colours of the annotation to be maintained in the exported image.
\par \pard\tx355  Note however that if colour is maintained you will lose up to 20 of the 256 grey levels in the exported image.
\par \pard\tx355 If Colour Merge is not selected the annotation colours will be mapped to grey levels and there will be no loss of image grey levels.
\par \page
{\up $}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up $} where to load}
{\up #}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up #} where_to_load}
\pard \b\fs36\cf1 Where to load
\par \plain\fs24 Define where to load the image by one of the following:
\par 
\par \{bmc bm1.bmp\} Drag the \uldb Import Selection Object\plain\fs24 {\v TIFF_Import_Object} to the required position.
\par \{bmc bm1.bmp\} Press the \b Centre\plain\fs24  button to centralise the load area.
\par \{bmc bm1.bmp\} Press the \b Origin\plain\fs24  button to position the load area at the origin
\par \{bmc bm1.bmp\} Enter the required screen co-ordinates and press the \b XY\plain\fs24  Button.
\par \page
